/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (Simulations have always become an important and complementary tool to test theories on galaxy formation and evolution. Simulations allow the researchers to generate and trace the evolution of a wide range of galactic morphologies.simulations can be used to predict properties of the observed systems that has not been detected, and to understand its formation process. When simulations do not match with observations, new theories need to be developed and implemented in the codes, in order to account for new physical processes. Also, observations have to be checked looking for possible observational biases.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
